{% if sys_units %}
{# SceneTrigger (zone_enter/exit) and WorldInteractable (trigger detection) both
   require a Collider(2D) ON THIS GAMEOBJECT to ever receive OnTrigger* callbacks —
   without one, _Systems has no collider and those micros are silently dead. #}
{% set sys_kinds = sys_units | map(attribute="kind") | list %}
{% set needs_sys_collider = "trigger" in sys_kinds or "interactable" in sys_kinds %}
{# Which DIMENSION that collider is has to agree with the trigger/interactable
   micros, and they do not read game_type directly — they read `dim_meta`
   (src/unity_compose.subsystems_for), which reports 3D for a non-embodied game
   whatever its declared dimension, because a UI board is a flat plane of 3D
   colliders and Collider2D has no Raycast(Ray) overload. Emitting a
   BoxCollider2D here for a 2d_topdown board therefore left [RequireComponent(
   typeof(Collider))] unsatisfied — Unity logged "has possibly missing Required
   Components" on _Systems and the click trigger never armed. One rule, spelled
   the same way in both places. #}
{# `default("walk")` because not every caller that renders this template supplies
   locomotion, and the honest reading of its absence is "nothing declared this
   game non-embodied" — which keeps every existing 2D project on the 2D collider
   it already had, byte for byte. #}
{% set sys_collider_is_2d = game_type in ("2D", "2d_topdown") and (locomotion | default("walk")) != "none" %}
